CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default-initialized array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ reverse order: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.dtor]/13: the elements of an array object of class type are
destroyed at the end of its lifetime, in the reverse order of
construction.  Goto conversion registered destructors only for objects
of class type, so a block-scope array's elements were never destroyed
(bin53; array members and delete[] were).  convert_decl now registers
the element destructors (array_destructor), also for multidimensional
arrays.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
